  "spots": [
    {
      "cell": [
        8,
        4
      ],
      "line": "The lead wagon's tailboard is carved with a road, and a gate across it, and a name rubbed out.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        16,
        9
      ],
      "line": "A ledger left on the step: towns, and what each was short of, in the same hand for twenty years.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        19,
        11
      ],
      "line": "A man's coat, folded in the tent and never worn, with salt in the seams.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        4,
        8
      ],
      "line": "Ruts, deep and old: the wagons have stood here before, and will again."
    }
  ],
  "people": [
    {
      "name": "Mother Ilse",
      "unit": "town_spice_seller",
      "cell": [
        13,
        6
      ],
      "facing": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "wander": 1,
      "chatter": [
        "Everything a rune wants, and nothing a rune doesn't. Feathers. Cord. A token from a grave nobody misses.",
        "We're gone at the next bell. Buy now or walk after us."
      ],
      "talk": {
        "hello": [
          "You've the look of folk who lay runes. Or want to. Come and see.",
          "Charms, makings, a bit of salt. Towns don't stock them; towns don't know what they're for."
        ],
        "again": "Still here? So are we, for now.",
        "ask": [
          {
            "q": "Where are you bound?",
            "a": "Wherever's short. A town runs out of salt and charms, and then it runs out of luck. We come before the luck goes."
          },
          {
            "q": "What's a rune want?",
            "a": "A charm to hold it and something green to wake it. A whetstone and herbs for the keen one. The rest you'll learn."
          }
        ],
        "sells": [
          {
            "item": "black_feather",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "knotted_cord",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "grave_token",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "whetstone",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "salt_pouch",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "climbing_rope"
          }
        ],
        "shop": "Dear, because I carried it. Worth it, because you can't get it anywhere else.",
        "sold": "Lay it well.",
        "bye": "Mind the road. It minds you back."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Corbin, who drives the oxen",
      "unit": "peasant",
      "cell": [
        9,
        8
      ],
      "facing": [
        1,
        0
      ],
      "wander": 2,
      "chatter": [
        "Twelve miles a day. Fourteen if the oxen like you. They don't like you.",
        "We've been held up three times this year. Twice it was wolves. Once it was a toll."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Hesk, who guards the wagons",
      "unit": "keep_watchman",
      "cell": [
        16,
        7
      ],
      "facing": [
        -1,
        0
      ],
      "wander": 2,
      "chatter": [
        "Keep your hands where Mother can see them. She's got eyes in the back of the wagon.",
        "The road's worse than it was. Things come out of the gates now and walk it."
      ]
    }
  ],
